# `go build ./cmd/jlp` drops a ~43MB binary named after the package in
# the repo root. Nothing covered it before, so a single `git add -A`
# would commit it — and this project has already had one cross-commit
# incident from exactly that command (see the Phase 4 ledger's
# one-writer policy). Anchored to the root so a future internal/jlp/
# directory is unaffected.
/jlp
